course: dictionary
lesson: 707
title: Working out a word with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. «Never use a stove, heater or barbecue inside a tent» is about heat and cooking, so here a barbecue is the metal grill, not a party.
explain: «The two streets finished the summer with one last football match and a barbecue, where the community officer burned all the sausages.» A street does not finish a summer with a grill, so this barbecue is the outdoor party. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it fits.
explain: «Burning charcoal gives off carbon monoxide, an invisible poisonous gas, so barbecues must never be brought indoors or into a tent.» The clues are burning and poisonous gas, so a barbecue is a thing that burns fuel to cook. When the meaning is still unclear, use a dictionary.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Barbecue» can be a noun (a metal grill, or an outdoor meal or party) or a verb (to cook food on a barbecue).
fact: «Barbie» is a friendly everyday name for a barbecue in Australia.
fact: «Carbon monoxide» is a poison gas you cannot smell, so barbecues must never be used indoors or in a tent.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «In Toronto, Sofia meets her dad's partner's two girls at a barbecue.» What is a barbecue here? | A stove for baking bread | A tent for sleeping in | A bus stop by the river | *An outdoor party where food is cooked on a grill
exercise: «Never use a stove, heater or barbecue inside a tent.» Why is this rule important? | Because barbecues make tents too cold | Because barbecues are too heavy to carry | Because tents are too small to hold food | *Because it can give off carbon monoxide, a poison gas
exercise: Dad will ____ the sausages tonight. Which word fits best? | tent | barbecue sauce | *barbecue | charcoal
test: «A sausage at a barbecue is mostly minced pork, and pork is meat from a pig.» What is pork? | A type of cheese | *Meat from a pig | A metal grill for cooking | Burning charcoal
test: «The two streets finished the summer with one last football match and a barbecue.» What does barbecue mean in this sentence? | *An outdoor party | A kind of football | A poison gas | A tent for camping
exam: «Burning charcoal gives off carbon monoxide, an invisible poisonous gas, so barbecues must never be brought indoors or into a tent.» Why must barbecues never be brought indoors? | Indoor rooms are too small for food | They are too heavy to lift up stairs | Their sauce makes the room smell bad | *Their poisonous gas can harm people
